---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../utils/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Get started | Krabka"
  description="Evaluate Krabka with browser experiments, local Kafka clients, compatibility checks, and an isolated staging cluster."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-left border-b border-white/10 pb-8 mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
        Get started
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-300">
        Explore Krabka in your browser, or try it with your Kafka applications. Choose a starting point below.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div id="evaluation-pathways" class="mb-14 grid items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-2">
        <section class="border-b border-white/10 pb-6" aria-labelledby="local-validation">
          <h2 id="local-validation" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Local and CI validation</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Check whether your application can produce and consume records with Krabka. Start a local broker, then connect your existing Kafka clients, kcat, or integration tests to <code>localhost:9092</code>. The quickstart covers setup and your first message exchange. Repeat your application's integration checks in CI to catch failures as it changes.</p>
          <a href={getPath('/docs/quickstart')} class="mt-3 inline-block text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Run the local quickstart</a>
        </section>
        <section id="compatibility" class="border-b border-white/10 py-6" aria-labelledby="preflight-check">
          <h2 id="preflight-check" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Preflight compatibility and parity check</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Identify compatibility gaps before you invest in a broader trial. Compare your workload's client versions, required Kafka APIs, and security settings with the support matrix and linked KIP coverage. Check the test evidence for your intended release, then identify unsupported features or behavior differences that need further evaluation.</p>
          <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/operations/support-matrix')} class="mt-3 inline-block text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Check the support matrix</a>
        </section>
        <section class="border-b border-white/10 pt-6 pb-6" aria-labelledby="staging-evaluation">
          <h2 id="staging-evaluation" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Non-disruptive staging evaluation</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Evaluate representative traffic on an isolated Krabka cluster while production clients stay on Kafka. Choose dual writes, MirrorMaker 2 replication, or shadow consumers to compare application behavior and results. Disable external side effects in trial consumers. Use the migration guide to review replication limits and consumer offsets before you plan a cutover.</p>
          <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/operations/migrate-from-kafka')} class="mt-3 inline-block text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Plan a staging evaluation</a>
        </section>
      </div>

      <aside class="frosted-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 p-6" aria-labelledby="browser-trial">
        <h2 id="browser-trial" class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Interactive sandbox</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Try Cluster Lab in your browser without a local installation.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">Explore KRaft consensus, replica failover, and fault injection with WebAssembly brokers.</p>
        <a href={getPath('/docs/lab/')} class="mt-6 inline-block rounded-lg bg-krab-600 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-krab-500">Open Cluster Lab</a>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-400">View-only on mobile. The simulation does not measure production throughput or disk durability.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <p id="clients" class="text-sm text-gray-300">For runnable client examples, <a href={getPath('/docs/quickstart#connect-your-application')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">connect your application in the quickstart</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
